IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026:
-- PART 11A (register of controllers, nominee directors and nominee shareholders), LAYER 1, first module:
-- s 386AA (application of the Part), s 386AB (interpretation) and s 386AC (meaning of "registrable").
--
-- READING A RESULT. A function here answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE of the thing asked):
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes, in its own words, on these facts;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no, in its own words (a "means" definition, a flat negative, an "other than", an "unless");
--   NOTHING     the text does not say (it lists without closing the list, says "includes", is silent, or limits a grant in its own wording).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every JUST FALSE branch carries `FALSE-kind` and the words that license it;
-- every NOTHING branch carries `NOTHING-kind` and why. The fork lines (F-...) are in NOTES.md, "Fork register (sgn)".
--
-- The Fourteenth Schedule, the Fifteenth Schedule and the Sixteenth Schedule are in another part's range. What they say is taken
-- as a fact, named for the fact and the Schedule. The Acts this Part points at (the Securities and Futures Act 2001, the Limited
-- Liability Partnerships Act 2005, the Trustees Act 1967, the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018) are likewise taken as facts.

§ `Section 386AA: application of this Part`

-- s 386AA(1)(a): the Part applies to all companies other than one set out in the Fourteenth Schedule.
-- src:25383 | 386AA.—(1) This Part applies to —
-- src:25385 | (a) all companies other than a company that is set out in the
-- src:25386 | Fourteenth Schedule; and
@ref s 386AA(1)(a) (src:25383-25386)
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AA(1)(a) this Part applies to the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the body is a company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (a) speaks of companies; a body that is not a company is for paragraph (b), and subsection (1) does not say "only"
    ELSE (IF `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all companies other than a company that is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- s 386AA(1)(b): the Part applies to all foreign companies registered under Division 2 of Part 11, other than one in the Fifteenth Schedule.
-- src:25383 | 386AA.—(1) This Part applies to —
-- src:25385 | (a) all companies other than a company that is set out in the
-- src:25386 | Fourteenth Schedule; and
-- src:25388 | (b) all foreign companies registered under Division 2 of
-- src:25389 | Part 11 other than a foreign company that is set out in the
-- src:25390 | Fifteenth Schedule.
@ref s 386AA(1)(b) (src:25383-25390)
GIVEN `the body is a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AA(1)(b) this Part applies to the foreign company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the body is a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (b) speaks of foreign companies registered under Division 2 of Part 11; a body that is not one is for paragraph (a), and subsection (1) does not say "only"
    ELSE (IF `the foreign company is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all foreign companies registered under Division 2 of Part 11 other than a foreign company that is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- s 386AA(1): the two paragraphs together. A body that is neither is outside both, and the subsection does not say "only" (fork F-AA1).
-- src:25383 | 386AA.—(1) This Part applies to —
-- src:25385 | (a) all companies other than a company that is set out in the
-- src:25386 | Fourteenth Schedule; and
-- src:25388 | (b) all foreign companies registered under Division 2 of
-- src:25389 | Part 11 other than a foreign company that is set out in the
-- src:25390 | Fifteenth Schedule.
@ref s 386AA(1) (src:25383-25390)
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AA(1) this Part applies to the company or foreign company` MEANS
    IF    `s 386AA(1)(a) this Part applies to the company` `the body is a company` `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 386AA(1)(b) this Part applies to the foreign company` `the body is a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` `the foreign company is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF    `s 386AA(1)(a) this Part applies to the company` `the body is a company` `the company is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             OR `s 386AA(1)(b) this Part applies to the foreign company` `the body is a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` `the foreign company is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the body is a company in the Fourteenth Schedule, or a foreign company in the Fifteenth Schedule, and the subsection excludes each ("other than ...")
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the body is neither a company nor a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11; the subsection lists two kinds of body and does not say "only"

-- s 386AA(1A): six provisions that bite a registrable controller even if the controller is itself in the Fourteenth or Fifteenth Schedule.
DECLARE `s 386AA(1A) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AA(1A) section 386AG(6)`
    `s 386AA(1A) section 386AH(6)`
    `s 386AA(1A) section 386AI(6)`
    `s 386AA(1A) section 386AIA(3)`
    `s 386AA(1A) section 386AJ`
    `s 386AA(1A) section 386AK`
    `s 386AA(1A) some other provision of this Part`

-- src:25394 | (1A) Despite subsection (1), sections 386AG(6), 386AH(6),
-- src:25395 | 386AI(6), 386AIA(3), 386AJ and 386AK apply to a person who is,
-- src:25396 | or of whom there are reasonable grounds to believe is, a registrable
-- src:25397 | controller of a company (other than a company that is set out in the
-- src:25398 | Fourteenth Schedule) or foreign company (other than a foreign
-- src:25399 | company that is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule), whether or not the
-- src:25400 | person is —
-- src:25402 | (a) a company that is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule; or
-- src:25404 | (b) a foreign company that is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule.
@ref s 386AA(1A) (src:25394-25404)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 386AA(1A) provision`
      `the person is, or there are reasonable grounds to believe the person is, a registrable controller of the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Part applies to that company or foreign company under section 386AA(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AA(1A) the provision applies to the person` MEANS
    IF    `the person is, or there are reasonable grounds to believe the person is, a registrable controller of the company or foreign company`
       AND `this Part applies to that company or foreign company under section 386AA(1)`
       AND (CONSIDER provision
            WHEN `s 386AA(1A) section 386AG(6)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 386AA(1A) section 386AH(6)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 386AA(1A) section 386AI(6)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 386AA(1A) section 386AIA(3)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 386AA(1A) section 386AJ` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 386AA(1A) section 386AK` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite subsection (1), sections 386AG(6), 386AH(6), 386AI(6), 386AIA(3), 386AJ and 386AK apply to a person who is ... a registrable controller" grants the application in that case, with no "only"; it says nothing of another provision or another person

-- s 386AA(2): the obligation to comply extends to all natural persons and to all entities. Residence, citizenship and where an entity is
-- formed or does business make no difference, so they are not inputs (finding 3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:25408 | (2) The obligation to comply with this Part extends to all natural
-- src:25409 | persons, whether resident in Singapore or not and whether citizens of
-- src:25410 | Singapore or not, and to all entities, whether formed, constituted or
-- src:25411 | carrying on business in Singapore or not.
@ref s 386AA(2) (src:25408-25411)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AA(2) the obligation to comply with this Part extends to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a natural person` OR `the person is an entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) names all natural persons and all entities; it says nothing of a person who is neither

-- s 386AA(3): the Part extends to acts and omissions outside Singapore.
-- src:25418 | (3) This Part extends to acts done or omitted to be done outside
-- src:25419 | Singapore.
@ref s 386AA(3) (src:25418-25419)
GIVEN `the act or omission was done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AA(3) this Part extends to the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission was done outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) says the Part extends to acts and omissions outside Singapore; it says nothing of one inside, which subsections (1) and (2) govern

§ `Section 386AB: interpretation of this Part`

-- "unless the context otherwise requires" opens the section; whether the context requires otherwise is a judgment the text leaves open, taken as a plain input (fork F-AB1).
-- src:25425 | 386AB. In this Part, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 386AB (src:25425-25425)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB the definitions of this Part apply here` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part, unless the context otherwise requires"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:25427 | “approved exchange” means an approved exchange as defined
-- src:25428 | in section 2(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001;
@ref s 386AB "approved exchange" (src:25427-25428)
GIVEN `the exchange is an approved exchange as defined in section 2(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "approved exchange" the exchange is an approved exchange` MEANS
    IF `the exchange is an approved exchange as defined in section 2(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“approved exchange” means an approved exchange as defined in section 2(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001"

-- "significant interest" and "significant control" are the Sixteenth Schedule's: that Schedule is in another part's range, so what it decides is a fact.
-- src:25485 | “significant interest”, in relation to a company or a foreign
-- src:25486 | company, has the meaning given in the Sixteenth Schedule.
@ref s 386AB "significant interest" (src:25485-25486)
GIVEN `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "significant interest" the person has a significant interest` MEANS
    IF `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“significant interest”, in relation to a company or a foreign company, has the meaning given in the Sixteenth Schedule" (a definition handed to a Schedule: ruling of 2026-11-05, "Delegated definitions", item (a))

-- src:25482 | “significant control”, in relation to a company or a foreign
-- src:25483 | company, has the meaning given in the Sixteenth Schedule;
@ref s 386AB "significant control" (src:25482-25483)
GIVEN `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "significant control" the person has significant control` MEANS
    IF `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“significant control”, in relation to a company or a foreign company, has the meaning given in the Sixteenth Schedule" (a definition handed to a Schedule: ruling of 2026-11-05, "Delegated definitions", item (a))

-- src:25443 | “legal entity” means any body corporate formed or incorporated
-- src:25444 | or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore and includes a
-- src:25445 | foreign company;
@ref s 386AB "legal entity" (src:25443-25445)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "legal entity" the body is a legal entity` MEANS
    IF `the body is a body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore` OR `the body is a foreign company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“legal entity” means any body corporate formed or incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore and includes a foreign company" (a "means" definition; the "includes" widens it by a foreign company, it does not open the list: fork F-AB2)

-- src:25433 | “corporate controller”, in relation to a company or a foreign
-- src:25434 | company, means a legal entity which has a significant interest
-- src:25435 | in, or significant control over, the company or the foreign
-- src:25436 | company, as the case may be;
@ref s 386AB "corporate controller" (src:25433-25436)
GIVEN `the person is a legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "corporate controller" the person is a corporate controller` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a legal entity`
       AND (   `s 386AB "significant interest" the person has a significant interest` `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `s 386AB "significant control" the person has significant control` `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corporate controller”, in relation to a company or a foreign company, means a legal entity which has a significant interest in, or significant control over, the company or the foreign company"

-- src:25438 | “individual controller”, in relation to a company or a foreign
-- src:25439 | company, means an individual who has a significant interest
-- src:25440 | in, or significant control over, the company or the foreign
-- src:25441 | company, as the case may be;
@ref s 386AB "individual controller" (src:25438-25441)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "individual controller" the person is an individual controller` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an individual`
       AND (   `s 386AB "significant interest" the person has a significant interest` `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `s 386AB "significant control" the person has significant control` `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“individual controller”, in relation to a company or a foreign company, means an individual who has a significant interest in, or significant control over, the company or the foreign company"

-- src:25430 | “controller” means an individual controller or a corporate
-- src:25431 | controller;
@ref s 386AB "controller" (src:25430-25431)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "controller" the person is a controller of the company or foreign company` MEANS
    IF    `s 386AB "individual controller" the person is an individual controller` `the person is an individual` `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 386AB "corporate controller" the person is a corporate controller` `the person is a legal entity` `the person has a significant interest in the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` `the person has significant control over the company or foreign company, as the Sixteenth Schedule gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“controller” means an individual controller or a corporate controller"

-- src:25447 | “limited liability partnership” has the meaning given by
-- src:25448 | section 4(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005;
@ref s 386AB "limited liability partnership" (src:25447-25448)
GIVEN `the partnership is a limited liability partnership as section 4(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "limited liability partnership" the partnership is a limited liability partnership` MEANS
    IF `the partnership is a limited liability partnership as section 4(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“limited liability partnership” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005" (a definition handed to another Act)

-- "member of the public" includes a member of the company (or foreign company) acting as such: the list is open, so off it the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:25450 | “member of the public” includes —
-- src:25452 | (a) in the case of a company — any member of the
-- src:25453 | company acting in the member’s capacity as such;
-- src:25454 | and
-- src:25456 | (b) in the case of a foreign company — any member of
-- src:25457 | the foreign company acting in the member’s capacity
-- src:25458 | as such;
@ref s 386AB "member of the public" (src:25450-25458)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company acting in the member's capacity as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the foreign company acting in the member's capacity as such` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "member of the public" the person is a member of the public` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company acting in the member's capacity as such` OR `the person is a member of the foreign company acting in the member's capacity as such`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“member of the public” includes (a) in the case of a company — any member of the company acting in the member's capacity as such; and (b) in the case of a foreign company — any member of the foreign company acting in the member's capacity as such" leaves the list open

-- "register of controllers" or "register": the register that the company is required to keep under s 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3);
-- for a foreign company, under s 386AF(4), (4A), (5) or (6).
DECLARE `s 386AB "register of controllers" kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AB "register of controllers" a company to which this Part applies`
    `s 386AB "register of controllers" a foreign company to which this Part applies`

-- src:25460 | “register of controllers” or “register” —
-- src:25462 | (a) in relation to a company to which this Part
-- src:25463 | applies — means the register that the company is
-- src:25468 | required to keep of its registrable controllers under
-- src:25469 | section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3); and
-- src:25473 | (b) in relation to a foreign company to which this Part
-- src:25474 | applies — means the register that the foreign
-- src:25475 | company is required to keep of its registrable
-- src:25476 | controllers under section 386AF(4), (4A), (5) or (6);
@ref s 386AB "register of controllers" (src:25460-25476)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 386AB "register of controllers" kind of body`
      `the register is the register of its registrable controllers that the company is required to keep under section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is the register of its registrable controllers that the foreign company is required to keep under section 386AF(4), (4A), (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AB "register of controllers" the register is the register of controllers` MEANS
    IF (CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 386AB "register of controllers" a company to which this Part applies` THEN `the register is the register of its registrable controllers that the company is required to keep under section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3)`
        WHEN `s 386AB "register of controllers" a foreign company to which this Part applies` THEN `the register is the register of its registrable controllers that the foreign company is required to keep under section 386AF(4), (4A), (5) or (6)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“register of controllers” or “register” — (a) in relation to a company to which this Part applies — means the register that the company is required to keep of its registrable controllers under section 386AF(1), (1A), (2) or (3); and (b) in relation to a foreign company ... under section 386AF(4), (4A), (5) or (6)"

§ `Section 386AC: meaning of "registrable"`

-- Paragraph (c): the controller B is one of eight kinds. Each kind is a constructor; a ninth stands for any other.
DECLARE `s 386AC(c) kind of controller B` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AC(c)(i) a company, or foreign company to which this Part applies, that is required to keep a register of controllers under section 386AF`
    `s 386AC(c)(ii) a company that is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule`
    `s 386AC(c)(iii) a foreign company that is set out in the Fifteenth Schedule`
    `s 386AC(c)(iv) a corporation whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange`
    `s 386AC(c)(v) a limited liability partnership to which Part 6A of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 applies, that is required to keep a register of controllers of limited liability partnerships under that Act`
    `s 386AC(c)(vi) a limited liability partnership that is set out in the Sixth Schedule to the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 386AC(c)(vii) a trustee of an express trust to which Part 7 of the Trustees Act 1967 applies`
    `s 386AC(c)(viii) a VCC`
    `s 386AC(c) none of those eight kinds`

-- src:25500 | (c) B (or each B if more than one) is either —
-- src:25502 | (i) a company, or foreign company to which this Part
-- src:25503 | applies, that is required to keep a register of
-- src:25504 | controllers under section 386AF;
-- src:25506 | (ii) a company that is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule;
-- src:25508 | (iii) a foreign company that is set out in the
-- src:25509 | Fifteenth Schedule;
-- src:25511 | (iv) a corporation which shares are listed for quotation on
-- src:25512 | an approved exchange;
-- src:25514 | (v) a limited liability partnership to which Part 6A of the
-- src:25515 | Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 applies, that
-- src:25516 | is required to keep a register of controllers of limited
-- src:25517 | liability partnerships under that Act;
-- src:25522 | (vi) a limited liability partnership that is set out in the
-- src:25523 | Sixth Schedule to the Limited Liability Partnerships
-- src:25524 | Act 2005;
-- src:25526 | (vii) a trustee of an express trust to which Part 7 of the
-- src:25527 | Trustees Act 1967 applies; or
-- src:25529 | (viii) a VCC.
@ref s 386AC(c) (src:25500-25529)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 386AC(c) kind of controller B`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 386AC(c) the controller is of a kind that paragraph (c) lists` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 386AC(c) none of those eight kinds` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 386AC: a controller (A) is registrable unless (a), (b) and (c) all hold. The "unless" is the text's own no (JUST FALSE); where it is not met
-- A is registrable (JUST TRUE); a person who is not a controller is outside the section (NOTHING).
-- src:25492 | 386AC. For the purposes of this Part, in relation to a company (X)
-- src:25493 | or a foreign company (X), a controller (A) is registrable unless —
-- src:25495 | (a) A’s significant interest in or significant control over X is
-- src:25496 | only through one or more controllers (B) of X;
-- src:25498 | (b) A is a controller of B (or each B if more than one); and
-- src:25500 | (c) B (or each B if more than one) is either —
-- src:25502 | (i) a company, or foreign company to which this Part
-- src:25503 | applies, that is required to keep a register of
-- src:25504 | controllers under section 386AF;
-- src:25506 | (ii) a company that is set out in the Fourteenth Schedule;
-- src:25508 | (iii) a foreign company that is set out in the
-- src:25509 | Fifteenth Schedule;
-- src:25511 | (iv) a corporation which shares are listed for quotation on
-- src:25512 | an approved exchange;
-- src:25514 | (v) a limited liability partnership to which Part 6A of the
-- src:25515 | Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 applies, that
-- src:25516 | is required to keep a register of controllers of limited
-- src:25517 | liability partnerships under that Act;
-- src:25522 | (vi) a limited liability partnership that is set out in the
-- src:25523 | Sixth Schedule to the Limited Liability Partnerships
-- src:25524 | Act 2005;
-- src:25526 | (vii) a trustee of an express trust to which Part 7 of the
-- src:25527 | Trustees Act 1967 applies; or
-- src:25529 | (viii) a VCC.
@ref s 386AC (src:25492-25529)
GIVEN `the person (A) is a controller of the company or foreign company (X)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A's significant interest in or significant control over X is only through one or more controllers (B) of X` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a controller of B (or of each B if more than one)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kinds of the controllers (B) through which A holds the interest` IS A LIST OF `s 386AC(c) kind of controller B`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AC the controller is registrable` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person (A) is a controller of the company or foreign company (X)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says when "a controller (A)" is registrable; it says nothing of a person who is not a controller
    ELSE (IF    `A's significant interest in or significant control over X is only through one or more controllers (B) of X`
            AND `A is a controller of B (or of each B if more than one)`
            AND (NOT (null `the kinds of the controllers (B) through which A holds the interest`))
            AND all (GIVEN b YIELD `s 386AC(c) the controller is of a kind that paragraph (c) lists` b) `the kinds of the controllers (B) through which A holds the interest`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a controller (A) is registrable unless — (a) A's significant interest in or significant control over X is only through one or more controllers (B) of X; (b) A is a controller of B (or each B if more than one); and (c) B (or each B if more than one) is either — (i) ... (viii) a VCC" (an "unless" that is met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
